              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rich"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It hit the spot! At first I thought the recipe called for an excessive amount of beef bouillon, but I tried the recipe as listed. It was delicious. With a little white rice added to each serving, and Crystal Hot Sauce at my side, the dish was wonderful. I'll be making it again.",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-28T13:20:54.043Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Qhhunters"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love all the fresh veggies in this recipe. We have been trying to amp up the veggies and cut down the meat and fish, so this recipe worked great. I did not add the pimientos, but did use a pinch of Chipotle Chili powder. Used organic everything, including Florida grown organic rice. Definitely will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-25T17:18:46.050Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mrs H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is awesome! Delicious! Husband and parents LOVE it! I give it a bit more flavor by sauteing the shrimp in butter with chopped garlic (the canned stuff is really easy), and adding about a teaspoon of cayenne to the mix. Sometimes I up the chili powder just a bit, but it really isn't necessary if you add the cayenne.",
            "datePublished": "2009-04-13T15:19:12.693Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "I Ferguson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved it! But to good from pretty good to great, it did need some extra seasoning. As others have said it needed a bit more seasoning. I seasoned the shrimp with garlic salt and black pepper. I also added a bay leave, red pepper flakes, and a splash of white wine to the sauce, then I let it simmer for twenty minutes longer. It was amazing.",
            "datePublished": "2008-09-02T16:28:14.780Z"
          },
